# Vulnerability Report: `op-chain-ops/srcmap/solutil.go`

## 1. Out-of-Bounds Slice Panic in `SourceMapTracer.OnOpCode`

### Vulnerability Summary
The `SourceMapTracer.OnOpCode` method can trigger a runtime panic (slice bounds out of range) when tracing EVM bytecode that contains a truncated `PUSH` instruction.

### Severity
* **Severity:** Medium
* **Impact:** Denial of Service (DoS) of the tracing/diagnostic infrastructure or node runner when executing transactions containing malformed or truncated bytecode.

### Detailed Description
In Go, slicing a slice beyond its length or capacity causes a runtime panic. In the `OnOpCode` method of `SourceMapTracer`, the tracer checks if an opcode is a `PUSH` operation:

```go
if op.IsPush() {
    var val []byte
    sc, ok := scope.(*vm.ScopeContext)
    if ok {
        start := pc + 1
        end := uint64(op) - uint64(vm.PUSH1) + 1
        val = sc.Contract.Code[start : start+end] // <--- Vulnerable Slicing
    }
```

If a contract has truncated bytecode (for example, ending with `PUSH2` `0x00` where the second push byte is missing), `len(sc.Contract.Code)` will be less than `start + end`. Slicing `sc.Contract.Code[start : start+end]` will trigger a Go panic, crashing the tracing execution flow.

### Impact
Any service, node RPC endpoint, or automated testing tool that utilizes `SourceMapTracer` to trace transactions can be forcefully terminated by an attacker deploying or executing a transaction with truncated contract bytecode.

### Proof of Concept / Affected Code Snippet
[op-chain-ops/srcmap/solutil.go#L290-L300](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/main/op-chain-ops/srcmap/solutil.go)

```go
	if op.IsPush() {
		var val []byte
		sc, ok := scope.(*vm.ScopeContext)
		if ok {
			start := pc + 1
			end := uint64(op) - uint64(vm.PUSH1) + 1
			val = sc.Contract.Code[start : start+end]
		} else {
			val = []byte("N/A")
		}
```

### Remediation
Ensure that the slice index boundaries are validated against the actual length of `sc.Contract.Code` before performing the slice operation:

```go
	if op.IsPush() {
		var val []byte
		sc, ok := scope.(*vm.ScopeContext)
		if ok {
			start := pc + 1
			pushLen := uint64(op) - uint64(vm.PUSH1) + 1
			codeLen := uint64(len(sc.Contract.Code))

			if start >= codeLen {
				val = []byte{}
			} else if start+pushLen > codeLen {
				val = sc.Contract.Code[start:]
			} else {
				val = sc.Contract.Code[start : start+pushLen]
			}
		} else {
			val = []byte("N/A")
		}
```

